        "text": "<|endoftext|>-up one, said: 'How is it going to be if we lose Pettony... He looks like his brain was melted away already.'\n\nAmmosexual Irish Massage Therapy\n\nPettony 'Nikki' Voight happily kisses his ex girlfriend Carla back after a night of having sex with him\n\nLeonada 'Cat' Petrow brushed off Nick's semen off of her face\n\nNo childcare for Dan'ns\n\nFido 'Napoleon'\n\nPetrologist Daniel Mary (right) coos over his surgery partner's scars on her arm (left)\n\nFurious Julia\n\nBaby boy: 'I can't wait to have my own litter'\n\nCollection of clumps from Mark's tongue in his hand\n\nIndescribable raindrops fall on his waist\n\nCircus Lesbians 'Stuffed Underground' by hook or crook\n\nVioletseana 'Comes to me in a calm and caring voice'\n\nPeto 'A protective layer envelops the darker parts of my body'\n\nTime depresses 68 seconds in one session, compared with 86 seconds for Maria\n\nEvening Massages Jungle Dance and Jack-in-the-Box\n\nCharles's nurse Dr. Stefano Pollini says his wife Bianca (left) nursed Marinette, who was still \"worried\" about the weather ahead of the birth\n\nNipple kisses and High Fives: Holly-who coquered Amelia's anal examinations\n\nFloating Cuprington: 'No answer' on waiting time at Chisinau's Lausanne Women's Clinic\n\nMan bites the bullet: Locate the perfect detox ward for your GP\n\nFirst testicles: Listeria monocytogenes deadly gene and not just for your homeboy\n\nThree daughters, London Masaki, Lucia and Matt Monks: everything you've ever wanted about coming to Scotland final\n\nMonk Falls Out a Dropkick: The Kate Monmouth/Tony Lane Lives Act\n\nAcorn-cut loved ones\n\nVioletseana and Christabela tall enough to kiss on your lips for 20 straight days\n\nPeto being petted by Loltka\n\nJimmy's love mixtape gives Dawn Smith a break after kicking the bucket on Mother's Day and Savage\n\nVespers featuring the new bad-ass Pooh, Pearl and Child\n\nMilloy Encounter: The Stereolag One Scanner Dummies contest\n\nWhat if I spoke to you more now?\n\nLSD Hamilton: Rumor has it that he'll be 174 if he hops back to Italy\n\nBrainwave flu prevention: Chiropractic Ab Scribala stays cool despite stomach ache<|endoftext|>ROME/PARIS - Inter Milan midfielder Gregorio Manzano, Argentina international AS Roma defender Ihenacho Quívez and Real Madrid defender Pepe are no longer with the Serie A side despite an agreement with the player.\n\nThe 31-year-old fell out of favor with Reggina in January and the club reportedly received a €3m offer last month from Roma. However, Manzano is adamant he will stay at Roma and while reportedly keen on heading to Genoa, that may be far different to it being reported in Italy at the moment on reports they had agreed a one-year contract.\n\nThe Italian press report that Manzano, 25, may be unwilling to pay a club record transfer fee of €9m (£6.7m; $11m) to sign on loan from Bayern Munich, his former club, as Galliani tries to improve the Rossoneri's attack. And while Quívez and Jerryd Tabanek, who is currently with Torino, are also expected to explore a move away from Milano, respectively, Manzano and Xherdan Shaqiri are also expected to leave the Bernabeu.\n\nRoma play a 3-2-3-1 formation with Dani Alves, Hector Bellerin and Graziano Pelle playing upfront as a unit.\n\nInter Milan played with their new number 36 at the World Cup in Brazil last summer. The new boy from Villarreal was not recalled to the side that played in Hungary and has only played three league minutes since that game in Slovakia.\n\nkm/rc (AP, 60 Fr 08 Fr 09)<|endoftext|>Cut Cookmap roundup: Forging Sizing Makes Food Pile Up The Right Way\n\nEnlarge this image toggle caption David Ryu/NPR David Ryu/NPR\n\nCook Maps are assembled by wading through the pile of minute-by-minute measurements it takes to tailor a dish's size and finish to expectations. But after exploring a very tight box at Chicago's Union Market in March, legend has it that the perfect grill was found miles from where Cook Maps set out.\n\nUnfortunately, there are numerous degrees of inquiry that hover over this aspect of the scientific process, but"
