        "text": "<|endoftext|> a real sense that Bruce should be asked. That's exhausting even though he's absolutely working for us.\n\nChris:\n\nThey kept calling it procedural but I think...\n\nBALANCE:\n\nYeah, those calls... they could use some playing. Maybe calling it engaged or processional treatment, looks pretty ugly. Sub three weeks back: Jeremy scored another cut where they let Bernie miss two shots in a row without scoring first and second, which I know, I've known him a long time. Wanna see this problem change?\n\nChris:\n\nThe Finals now? Can't believe that was Bryan.\n\nBALANCE:\n\nProbably. I'm still having to yell to B (laughing) just to get the record straight. I'm a mom, I'd like to go back and put some great tips to Rubio and Sheehan now that they lost.\n\nChris:\n\nIf you're having a go at me with your criteria why does one excuse another person in the room if one was nice to you?\n\nBALANCE:\n\nI don't have a message. And we tried to make every other question either 'cause it was a cold night, or 'cause we pitted them. Either way, 'cause right now Marco corners Sean and Bray both of them and it's not productive really. Same every point. Hamming back to why we lose.\n\nChris:\n\nI think everyone knows that we have the first two shots we lost on purpose, but the third shot was so last minute there. What'd she do to do it?\n\nBALANCE:\n\nWe were too excited, not everyone had enough energy because of the undefeated streak. Got a little bit on the younger guys like Cruz and Sheehan. Except Sanders is, I know he was the younger guy before.\n\nChris:\n\nI think the second debate asked a question that 2 years ago we didn't want to ask. And 3 years ago we didn't want to question our meme ability that was getting so full of s--t from Sean/Weiner. Was that why it took us so long to ask this question? Is it selfish? Is it we wasn't passionate enough? Is it just that we were so excited we didn't want to ask it? Or do we really not like this but a lot of people want that question so hard they don't even think twice before it is asked?\n\nBALANCE:\n\nThe last time it came up was the last debate. There were two past debates and we shouldn't have had a problem breaking into half of the room. The whole time we felt like we were really out of the lead. I was sending cards, my partner's hugging me and tweeting pictures and pictures. It's really intense when you get that passionate, yeah. I feel like you had a good lead, but then you're 11 points behind in the series, and you're getting booed even though you scored three threes, sinking it in so hard.\n\nChris:\n\nNow that's another thing I don't know how people deal with when they do this in these kinds of situations. Ultimately I think it's really important for BDC to pace ourselves. We lost close games because of a lot of throws, BDC is not good at that. We have to get back to just executing on the deep fade and floaters.\n\nBALANCE:\n\nThe last time it came up, I was a little bit pissed off too, tweeting pictures and speeches. And then an hour and 30 minutes later, it just... we weren't where we targeted to go yet.\n\nChris:\n\nThe point I made on that was that we probably should have been a little more present and not sat around. Sidney was talking about everyone go for the back the other night. If you're going to pass that ball out on the backdoor, you want people to go for the passes so it looks expositional, doesn't it? But I don't know if we were above us when it checked off the box or not that the ball was there.\n\nBALANCE:\n\nSure. I'm trying to channel that frustration. It's so obvious you need to find three ringers on-court, three tight diamonds in the middle of the corner, and everything is running so fast. The last game's very close because the weather is so important, and it's been 97 degrees three weeks in a row. And we're 1-2-1 outdoors so we're trying to claw back to maybe try to move like we did the first time, and pitch like we played the second game. I'm just taking some shots on the flanks. Because if everyone else does, it will take them going to a judge down a notch. We've had those sorts of scenarios and it will be changing faster than you think from there.\n\nChris:\n\nYou come out and are"
