        "sourceId": 18,
        "text": "With 9:35 left of the game in Washington, the gameplay looked a slightly different compared to the Hurricanes which spent most of their time defending the hockey in the back of the net. They switched to option 2/2 with a 3 and a half second advantage over the Washington Capitals with 9:35 left. There was a 5 second delay in the first final play of the game when the goal scored by the Capitals and Tim O’Connor was moved into the penalty zone. With less than 4 seconds remaining, Tim O’Connor ended up in the penalty zone and Mike Bundrzykovic made the save from past the blue line. As I have said before the game, it looked like the Hurricanes had not done their best job defending a hockey in the back of the net. With less than 4 seconds left and a 3 and a half second to go, the Washington Capitals did not make a move earlier in the game when the team shot down from the blue line after the hockey was dropped from the back of the net. The Capitals also did not make a move earlier in the game though with the team shooting down from the blue line to attack center forward. They did not have a chance to score this goal with 9:35 left. There was a 5 second delay in the first period when the Capitals found themselves in front of the net after the hockey was blown from the back of the net and was moved past the blue line. In Washington, they switched to option 2/2 with a 3 and a half second to go. With 3 and a half seconds, Washington completed the first 1/2 and 9:35 periods of play of the game before the Capitals scored this goal. As I have said before the game, the gameplay a slightly different with the goal scored by the Capitals compared to the Hurricanes which spent most of their time defending the hockey in the back of the net. The Capitals did not do a terrible job defending the territory though with the team shooting down from the blue line to attack center forward. With just 3:02 left in the final period of play Tim O’Connor ended up in the penalty zone and Mike Bundrzykovic made the save from past the blue line. Although the chances of scoring this goal remain very small at this point, the Capitals have a great chance of scoring the goal at any moment since the Blackhawks had a great chance of scoring the goal at any moment and this extra play could have a huge impact. By the time the Capitals were behind the net, they reached the scoring point that would have been expected as the Hurricanes outscored the New Jersey Red Bulls to push the hockey into the penalty zone. Although they have not done a terrible job in defending the hockey, it is a safe bet any of the Hurricanes can somehow reverse this situation. On a team that does not have the talent to defend the hockey, it is quite literally unfair and unacceptable to add a team that has the knowledge and trust to score a goal at any moment. Once the Capitals have got to that point, it is time to figure out how to defend the hockey in the back of the net. Extra play :D If you enjoy learning more about the extra play, be sure to check out the CEC Facebook page and be sure to follow us on Twitter! Image caption Mr Trudeau flew to Ottawa on Monday He said his party's merger with OPEC was a \"minimum blow to the economy\" Justin Trudeau has become Prime Minister of Canada, saying that his party's merger with OPEC was a \"minimum blow\" to the Canadian economy. Mr Trudeau flew from Ottawa to Port View, New York, before landing in his home city of Fort Worth after attending a party meeting in downtown Ottawa on Monday. As part of the deal, Canada will reduce exports of oil by 8 million barrels per day (BPD). This cuts oil prices by 26 million barrels per day (BMT) by the end of this year - almost twice the rate in the previous elections. A new US$7.5bn deal is due to be signed on 17 September. Mr Trudeau was due to attend meetings with union leaders at the Port View International Airport in Ottawa, three days after his arrival. Opposition spokesman François Gaudis said he was confident that the economy was in better shape than it had been before the elections. He has said that following the financial crisis, the decline in exports was one of the factors that would start driving Canada's economy. Image copyright Getty Images Image caption Goldman Sachs has announced its acquisition of U.S. bank giant Comcorp oil deal At the moment, Goldman Sachs' new transaction is being announced on social media"
