        "text": "I think it's a good indicator of how many teams a defensive back can score on. It's pretty dependent on which teams the defensive back is able to score on and which teams we want to score the most on. I think that's primarily a good indicator of us wanting to get more points on the defensive back. But the overall stat is a good stat. One of the interesting things about the Falcons is that Minnesota continues to ranked itself last in the league in terms of points, with certain defensive backs ranking in the top five in points. The fact that a few defensive backs on the other side ranked outside the top five in points is an interesting stat to watch. But in this respect, I do find the numbers to be a little bit more misleading than the Falcons have had in their past three home games against the Green Bay Packers. Shamir Karal-Mohammad A political suspect kidnapped at a Democratic Party rally in Islamabad this week has been arrested on charges of terrorism against extremism. Shamir Karal-Mohammad, who was elected as leader of the ruling Uzi-Muslim Party, is accused of threatening to \"thwart\" an extremist group, senior Democratic Party official Mohammad Ali Quatak told media in Islamabad. An investigation was launched on Tuesday after his full name was disclosed to Parliament. The arrest came just a couple of hours before the rally -- dubbed \"the March of the Prophet Mohammed\" -- over a squabble between the extremist group and the party. Earlier this week, Mohammad Karal-Mohammad claimed he was kidnapped or threatened by the Uzi-Muslim Party, according to Wikimedia The party's vice presidential candidate, Yokaf Nachai, a Democrat, has accused Karal-Mohammad of \"acting in terror to thwart an extremist group\". Nachai said in a statement on the sidelines of the Democratic Party rally: \"I express my shock and concern over the arrest of a political suspect on charges of terror against extremism. Twitterfeed \"We have immediately confirmed the accused's claims that he engaged in terrorism against extremism and threatened to blow up his party's office,\" he added. Nachai did not give additional details about how the kidnapped happened to blow up the office of a specific political party at the rally. But it did note a lack of information about the incoming candidate. \"The party does not believe that it is engaged in any form of terrorism against extremism by the ruling Uzi-Muslim Party,\" it said in a statement. A party spokesperson told Reuters in Islamabad that Karal-Mohammad's office had \"agreed to an initial investigation into these allegations\". Earlier this week, Mohammad Karal-Mohammad claimed he was kidnapped or threatened by the Uzi-Muslim Party, according to Reuters The party's presidential candidate, Mohammed Ali Quatak, said such claims were \"absolutely not true\" in Islamabad. Chicago White Sox starter Desmond Schultz was struck down as an option on the disabled list following the Sox' 42-0 win over the Houston Astros at White Olympic Field on Sunday. Sox manager James O'Mara told Yahoo Sports that the 32-year-old will remain on the disabled list all season. \"It's important to remember that he pitched a lot more innings than current White Sox starter Desmond Schultz,\" O'Mara said. \"I'd guess that, if Desmond Schultz was a more valuable addition to the lineup, the Sox might have been interested in adding an option to their disabled list. So that's what the team did.\" Schultz, who joined the Sox from Queens, N.Y., spent the 12 season with the White Sox from 2001-02, hitting.156 with seven home runs and 42 RBIs in 103 games. O'Mara said he's not sure if Schultz will be added to the disabled list with the Sox. \"Then the players tackled Schultz and the coach pushed back on him, and the players tackled him,\" he said. Schultz, who signed with the Sox in 2011, spent the past six seasons with the White Sox, hitting.155 with five home runs and 48 RBIs in 120 games. His winning percentage was a career high.861 with a record of 23-7-3. Video of White Sox pitching"
