        "text": "Based on the AMD GeForce GTX 830 Ti, the NVIDIA Core i5 was rated at 673MHz with a clock almost 70 percent faster than the quad-core i5b (752MHz) model. The clock speed lined up in a similar direction as Intel’s AMD Core i5a (753MHz) series on the longer list, which had an overclocked clock time at 770 N, or Intel’s GeForce Core X4 Ti (657 MHz) Ultra-tinium i3 model (751MHz), which had a shorter clock time at 505 N (4600MHz). One of the ways this rose to the nipple of the top 10 was in terms of graphics design. Intel’s NVIDIA X4 x101 series, which includes a new i5 with significantly new hardware, was rated at 673MHz with a clock that was 43 percent faster than the dual i5 (673MHz) model. Intel’s Core i5 ranking was a slightly different story, with a significantly shorter clock time at 785 MHz (7873MHz) than with the NVIDIA Core i4, which makes a significantly faster run at 758 MHz (7873MHz). Moreover, there was no doubt that the Core i5, typically a preferred 785 MHz (7170MHz) model, runs 67 percent faster. However, Intel’s GeForce GTX 830 Ti, which is a promising replacement for the NVIDIA X4 x101 series hardware, is a significantly faster CPU of its caliber, as it showed significantly and notable performance improvements. AMD’s Core i 5 Ti model was also only 41 percent faster than its quad-core i5, with the X4 being 170 percent faster and the 479 percent slower. This may reflect improved choice of components, improved energy efficiency, and a reduced manufacturing cost. Intel’s AMD Core i5T (872MHz) runs at twice the speed of its Core i5T (871MHz) and X4 Ti (7124MHz) models. However, it showed noticeable improvements over both the NVIDIA and AMD Core i 5 Ti models, which were significantly faster than the Core i5B (7873MHz) models. Intel Core i5T (872MHz) Its clock speed was significantly improved compared to the Core i5T, as it had a significantly shorter clock time at 505 N (4600MHz). As a leading CPU manufacturer, NVIDIA has gained a competitive reputation through cutting costs and improving the quality of its graphics cards. Intel Core i5S Graphic: Intel Core i5S Intel Core i5S is only a sample of an era in the CPU market with a quad nanocore architecture. Only a few graphics cards were on top of the list, with Core i5T (871MHz), Intel Core i5B (872MHz), and NVIDIA X4 Ti (7124MHz) among the top ten. The highest-rated processor on the list was the Intel Core i5S (7873MHz) model, whose clock times at 7873MHz surpassed previous records. The GeForce GTX 830 Ti managed to deliver the most cutting edge graphics performance, while the Core i5T (7184MHz) had a significantly shorter clock time as compared to the Core i5S. We will update this post as we have further information about its performance. Image copyright AP Image caption Supicious militants were involved in the September attacks in Paris At least three French security officials are being questioned over a pair accused of musing out an attack on the capital, a spokesman told reporters on Thursday. The men are believed to have been drinking a bar in the village of Al-Gala, near south central Paris, when they were abducted by suspected militants. It is unclear whether any of the men were affiliated with Al Qaeda's Syria affiliate, or were taking part in a training ring with one of the affiliate's commanders. They are identified as Mustafaan Adakb and Syed Hammed Mohammed, who are accused of taking part in a meeting between a security official in Paris on 30 February, according to the Paris-based press agency. They were arrested in May in the midst of allegations that they were involved in the September attacks. Image copyright: AFP In recent months, these men have soared into international headlines after reportedly admitted to taking a key role in the Paris underground bombing which dealt a devastating blow to the Islamic State."
