        "text": "It is looking to be a contentious start to the season, but Di Pedro has some new indicators to show that he could become one of the big names next year. The Old Trafford Bridge transfer is one of the club's top ten signings for 2014, ranked at No. 11 on the club's single-day Matchboard Online rankings. Setting up for Saturday's 2-1 win at Sverreal Madrid, the Taiwanese also changed his game for the first time in the Gunners' tantalising 2-1 knockout win at Manchester United on Saturday. After registering three goals in his final 90 minutes for the fellow London club in the competition, it seems di Pedro is ready to get back up to the first team next year or later. The 20-year-old France international scored just the fourth goal of his campaign against Liverpool and Mourinho has tipped on his return to the Premier League next year. Rio Di Pedro seems focused on playing a bit of a part in his upcoming campaign after he scored just the fourth goal in 90 minutes in a 2-1 victory at Manchester United on Saturday. Rio Di Pedro was on Jose Mourinho's disabled first-team roster on Monday after starting his 17th game for the Gunners and adding three goals and five assists in his final 92 appearances for the Gunners. But the 20-year-old Mexico City international, who agreed a four-year deal with Spurs last month to get back up to the first team, said it was his best performance of the season. \"I've played in the Premier League since I was 18 years old and played in a different role than the other teams in the competition,\" Di Pedro said. \"At this stage I am still going to play a lot in the first team. But if I stay fit I have a pretty good shot at getting into the first team. \"I am not yet an expert at this stage but I will be ready to get into the first team and I will be capable of contributing more at this stage.\" The 24-year-old has not been able to build on his first-team performances in last Saturday's 3-0 win over Manchester City at a slender pace. But he says he is slowly getting back to his original form after his back injury. The France international started his 17th game this week and scored just the fourth goal of his campaign for Manchester United before starting on Saturday's 1-1 win over City. Di Pedro said: \"I am playing really well and I may not have a whole lot of energy in there yet but I am in pretty good shape too. \"Agains Sverreal Madrid I scored goals in a 2-1 win but I am safe to say I am playing really well and I am in pretty good shape. \"Again Liverpool I played pretty well but I still have got a lot of energy and I am preparing to get into the first team. \"I am playing really well and I will not only be able to contribute but also look really good next year.\" There’s a storyline in the game where you confront a main character and master a feat of some sort. I’ve been following Doctors Without Borders for quite a long time now, but I really enjoyed the storyline & the end of a match, and it’s going to be awesome. At the end of the game, you get to meet a better character than I have ever met in what happens to be a Trampout monster. A lot of fans have given up on the new boss because of the enigmatic nature of the main character but the biggest disappointment you end up with is that you are fighting the guy hard. Don’t get me wrong this is going to be an easy battle, but there’s going to be a ton of fun in the end and you aren’t going to give up on really simple, easy-to-master tasks such as making costumes, filling & loading boxes etc or something. I’ll give you this... The number of women visiting the United States declines 10,018 in 2004 The number of women who travel on the holidays to the United States declined from 10,018 in 2004 to 14,85 in 2006. An independent analysis of the numbers from the United States Office of Management and Budget found the number of women visiting the United States declined from 14,85 in 2004 to 14,852 in 2006. This is among the largest decline in history because the number of women visiting abroad An independent analysis of the numbers from the United States Office of Management and Budget found the number of women visiting the United States declined from 10,018 in 2004 to 14,852 in 2006. This is among the largest decline in history because the number of women visiting abroad is in the third quarter Source: Wikimedia Commons."
