        "sourceId": 640,
        "text": "Being either a good goalkeeper or a midfielder will always be a negative experience, especially for a goalkeeper who is either a bad defender or a poor midfielder. But if you’re using a risky midfielder, you probably want a second-round pick. Then again, for a poor midfielder, he might not be a good first pick. Also, he might not be able to be a good defender for far too long, and he gets a third-round pick far too soon. WASHINGTON -- \"President Trump will veto the Affordable Care Act, as best I can tell,\" his attorney general's office said in a news release. \"I cannot favor vetoing the bill because he's the type of pebblebag the Democrats want to block.\" ADVERTISEMENT When deciding which legislation, Democrats have said they will veto changes in health care law unanimously, and the attorney general's office describes the move as \"a landslide.\" Senate Minority Leader Mitch McConnell (D-Conn.), Jeff Nuske (D-Md.) and Jason Chaffetz (D-Ill.) are cosponsors of veto bill, as are House Minority Whip Chuck Schumer (D-N.J.). MacRuffy, a top House Republican, will veto, and nor will Donald Trump Donald John TrumpREAUSE: Lobists urge Trump block Huawei products from electric grid | Ex-security officials condemn Trump's emergency declaration | malicious cybertool found | Facebook faces questions on treatment of moderators Key senators say administration should exclude Huawei in electric tech MORE's office told CNN News that it would be up to his office whether to favor a change in federal health care law. WASHINGTON (CNN) -- The member of the House party who made remarks strenuously critical of former President Barack Obama has said he was not involved in a violent schism with the Democrats. \"I am glad that Minority Leader Nancy Pelosi (R-Cal.) is not involved in a violent schism with the Democrats,\" Pelosi said in an interview on CNN's \"This Week.\" He also pointed out Trump's trust with the Democrats is running low. \"I don't even trust the Democrats,\" Pelosi said. \"It's not like it's easy for me to live in Washington. I don't trust the Democrats, period.\" Pelosi said he was \"deeply concerned\" about the connection between Trump's comments about immigrants and his criticisms of the President, adding: \"I don't even understand that.\" In an interview on CNN's \"This Week,\" he said he was \"damaged\" by Trump's comments during a news conference at the White House Hotel in Washington D.C. But Pelosi said after the conference concluded he had to ask himself whether Trump has said \"anything about immigrants.\" \"The President has been highly critical over the past several weeks for saying that immigrants are in a recession,\" he said. \"The President has most definitely been saying, among other things... that Hispanics are in a recession.\" Trump, the GOP vice presidential nominee, last week slammed the anti-immigrant rights group Family Foundation, accusing him of saying that he would use the word \"immigrant\" instead of \"hat shirt.\" Although Trump has repeatedly maintained that Obama's statements were incorrect, it was unclear at the time whether he would ever be prosecuted for saying something that was incorrect. Pelosi said the President's comments made Republicans justified to think about what Trump told them. \"The President's made Republicans to think about what Trump told them,\" he said. \"The President has been highly critical over the past several weeks for saying, among other things, 'I don't even understand that.' when I say Hispanics are in a recession.\" Pelosi said he was \"disappointed\" by Trump's comments about the controversy over immigration. \"The President has not said a single word about immigrants,\" he said in a statement. \"As a Democratic presidential candidate, as a D since 1993 and now an independent, the President has needlessly shown off his courage, determination and demeanor in appealing to the overwhelming majority of immigrants, especially those who are in a highly volatile economy.\" Pelosi was asked to answer questions about Trump's comments during the July 15 news conference, one of several slated for the final 100 days of Trump's presidency. New features"
