        "text": "This week we’ve excitedly announcing the release of the AppleBook iOS 6.0 update. This new update adds some of the most powerful features to the original version of the device with the overall success we’ve been expecting coming from the improvements available on the device. As expected, as a result of Apple’s recent improvement efforts, you can see that Apple is pulling off some of their biggest and best improvements. We’ve been happy to see a lot of the value that improvements have come out of Apple’s existing products; however, we’re looking forward to a lot of updates being available throughout 2017. Additionally, those who have already used the Apple Note 7 on their AppleBook 6 or iPad should not wait for copies of this version from the Apple Watch app. While there are still major lacks regarding the Note 7, we’d like to update you with the news that Apple will begin to release updates to the Note 7 for new devices in the next few weeks, starting early 2017. Apple announced earlier this week that it won’t release all device updates until at least 2017, and that some further updates will likely be available in the meantime. The AppleBook iOS 5.11 (news Update) is available right now, as well as many other improvements to this model, including very smaller improvements in the screen and added facial recognition features. We’ll get into many more details in the coming weeks as well as for additional information, but we urge you not to wait a few weeks for a complete Apple Note 7 review. Lastly, those who already used the Note 7 on their AppleBook 6 or iPad should not wait to buy a copy of this version. Apple already has a state-of-the-art smartwatch that can control the AppleBook 6 or iPad remotely onto the screen and view interactive content by using the headset for your smart TV. Now, if you’re like us, the company will be introducing a new design, dug out by Alex Kafkin and Eric Schneider. The incredible size of the Note 7 will make it easy to watch TV, sports, movies and movies directly from behind or outside, or from your laptop. The screen measures at an 13.6”x11.6.5” KHD80 resolution for greater clarity and faster sharpening, allowing you to zoom the device onto the screen more quickly with your finger. You can touch it using its power supply more easily than on previous watch devices, but it’s unlike what you’ll find on smartwatch, where the smartwatch port and power supply can function for more than an hour. In addition to its size, the Note 7 also offers far easier remote control than its predecessor smartwatch, where users can use it to access a watch from home or to communicate remotely with a dedicated smart TV. While it’s a smaller device that will have the same features as its AppleBook 5 or AppleBook 6 counterpart, we expect its larger size and unique packaging will help the Note become the company’s most popular smartwatch. Its plusful design, flexibility and affordability will ultimately make it one of our go-to smartwatch. The Note 7 returns for pre a trial at Apple’s Apple Store on October 11th. Customers participating in the trial get a pre-order price of up to $9,000 for the trial and are able to purchase copies of the Apple Note 7 for up to $34.99. A trial trial will be available on Apple’s Absolute Price app for a 10% discount on October 11th at the Apple Store. Where do you expect to see the Note 7 hit retail shelves? We have the answer for you. The Note 7 will be sold under the name of Honda Associates Group, and it will be manufactured by a parent division of Yamaha Associates Group. This lets users easily access all of Apple’s cutting-edge technology products, as well as its in-house facial recognition system. However, it will only get smaller as the company continues to monetize. From the Note’s improved display design and unique video content to an integrated focus bar on the back, the main goal of the Note 7 is to set the device up as one of the most innovative devices in today’s consumer industry. After its first year on the market the Note 7 will feature an upgrade to 1920p resolution, which is probably not long in the works yet, but we expect to see customers buy an increasing range of copies in the coming years. Another notable feature from the Note 7 will be a new Apple Watch which allows users to control the device in a headset. This will mark Apple’s first major line of smartwatch and begin to establish itself as one of its recognizable smartwatch makers. BEIJING (Reuters) - A roadside bomb landed on a road outside a propanefuel power plant in Hong Kong last week and allegedly killed at least two people, a Hong Kong official said on Thursday."
