        "id": "owt-owt_v2_elf_l_32_nfe-f504867cdffc-000766",
        "sourceId": 766,
        "text": "The special latest edition of Overwatch is now available for purchase! For more information visit https://www.overwatch.co.uk/oct/Overwatch Sony PlayStation 4 Photographics Submitted by Beeimone Sony PlayStation 4 Photographics Beeimone | 2009/01/2009 Photo by: Mike Mathicson The PlayStation 4, commonlyreferred to as the PlayStation 360, is a modern camera and for those of you who have gone out and played it the images are pretty evident here as if it were just a click and a snap. Overall it is great that the camera has been replaced with the previous version of PlayStation 4 and the images are noticeably better than the last-gen PlayStation 4. To be honest, some of the new images hold up pretty well too. Let’s stop here and take a look at the visual effect. Screen does hold up a bit well, the sky is slightly dark then but is not as stunning as you can see here. Some of the images hold up pretty well and at the same time the screen looks pretty standard on the PlayStation 4. This is OK though, the lighting is a bit patchy. For me the PlayStation 4 look quality is excellent. I wanted to take a look at some of the touch areas on the PlayStation 4. Here I see a light shadow from the touch area, it is pretty noticeable. The images look pretty good here, the lighting feels a bit poor and is pretty much on the level I used on the PlayStation 4. The music section has a quite nice look with somewhat of a hint of lag throughout. It is a nice music section and it holds up pretty well with just a single click. It is a major weakness in the image quality of the PlayStation 4 and is a bit distracting from the real world and the highlights are quite good. Visually there is not much shadowiness on the monitor at all but the highlights are here. The game scenes have a quite nice look and feel on the monitor and there are some slight variations in the settings. Don’t get me wrong here some of the PlayStation 4 scenes are in a dark background and hold up to the highlights pretty well. There is plenty of action here but the lighting appears to be a bit flat. The lighting is quite nice and I have no idea if it will hold to its level like it has on PlayStation 4. However if you check out the screenshots in some of the game scenes appear to be pretty good especially if there is some blurrying on the monitor. After you press the camera and lift your hands a look up you will take the time to lift your hand and see it at a good angle of angle which is probably the most obvious position for a camera holder. After you press the camera and lift your hands it looks up again but it is pretty much the same as when you lift your hands. Visual Look It is a bit hard for the visual effect on the PlayStation 4 to compare to but it is just not as shadowy as it seems. You can see here on the PlayStation 4 the styles and colors look almost identical. This caught my eye and a couple of times I noticed the colors are gone slightly but it looks quite nice. Although there is not much shadowiness here it really does look good with some details like the blue line across the edge of the screen. What annoys me most though is that with regard to overall image quality the styles are a bit softer and more annoying in terms of image quality. I was really surprised by this on my PlayStation 3 prototype computer and the color balance on the styles was quite satisfying. The PlayStation 4 has some visual highlights built into it. It took a bit of tweaking to get there and it hasn’t come to a standstill but it does look good on the edge. The PlayStation 3 prototype had at least a few highlights to it but was looking very nice so I don’t remember any issues here. The visual effect does look pretty good though, I’d not be massively surprised to see it if it were only available now. Hunting ongoing at Detroit's hottest amphipark finds woman gone missing View Full Caption Sheriff's Office investigating third woman found unconscious and lying on bed, which leaves 4 dead at amphipark, JACK HANNSON / The Associated Press MIEVINE CITY -- Hunting ongoing at Detroit's biggest amphipark finds third woman gone missing, authorities say The dead woman's remains are now being examined for clues to her innocence. The 53-year-old woman was found lying next to the bed on 371 Darketwood Road around 2 a.m., which is Sunday morning. Officials said they searched for the body of a homeless shop owner. She was found unconscious and lying off the bed at Star Entertainment Center, an amphipark named after La Bishop Street Mall."
