        "sourceId": 935,
        "text": "The advantage of the app is that it can interact with your phone, and can be controlled directly via Bluetooth. At the moment in iOS 8, the app is not a single controller, but rather just a single back button that interacts with your phone. The app allows users to switch between different touch modes - for example, you might have the option to tap \"Save Play\" or \"Download\" to record your video - by selecting the options and tapping the Edit button. It also features a feature called \"Play Now,\" so you can set the app to different modes depending on what video you are recording on your phone. The app also features tweaks, such as \"Set Up Settings and Save Photos and Video,\" and \"Set Up Privacy and Save Your Video.\" All these give users the ability to share and share videos recorded on the app with their smartphone. TOKYO - This week, a joint team of plastic architects at the National Laboratory, Kaoicha, Japan unveiled six new ways of making solid plastic replicas, which will allow them to be extracted and used in making medical devices, further reducing the risk of leukemia. \"Along with the joint team, as part of a six-month development plan, a joint team completed the successful manufacturing of architectural replicas which could be converted into high-quality plastics in an attempt to further begin this project,\" said Yoko Takoya, a plastic architect at the National Laboratory, Hong Kong. This is the first time fully-temperatured plastic replicas have been manufactured at an approximate temperature of 70° to 150°C on a plastic decorations. In addition to the additional challenge of making solid plastic replicas, two more plastic replicas have been successfully manufactured in just six months. At this early stage, there are still a number of important measures still to be put in place, such as the methods by which replicas are manufactured, as well as the design of the material, which could be used in the manufacturing of medical devices and even emergency devices. \"Here are some important benefits of allowing the replicas to be produced simultaneously while minimizing the risk of having to bethrown away during the process, among other benefits such as weight, solidity, and flat surface size,\" said Takoya. \"However, we know that manufacturing is still in its initial stages, and we have the hope that it could soon be converted into a solid plastic.\" Takoya's team is also working on a process whereby manufactured replicas are assembled using a chemical material known as a nanoparticle. As part of this process, further replicas are to be created making use of existing materials. \"The build-up of such processes by which replicas are assembled on intact plastic decorationss could prove very useful in treating and reducing the spread of type I leukemia and improving the treatment of it,\" said the National Laboratory, Tokyo. These replicas are also used to manufacture glue and foam decorationss. Watch : development video: New York's Sukyby Avenue Fire Department says 911 service will remain active in downtown Manhattan starting Friday. NEW YORK (NC) — As the cries continue to rise, New York's Fire Department has resumed the active 911 service throughout downtown Manhattan starting Friday. 911s will remain suspended until 9 a.m. because of the Independence Street fire that pitched the neighborhood on Tuesday. The Manhattan's National Office of Fire said the department's evacuations are more intense than they were before the Independence Street terrorist attacks, and the number of fire centers in the area is \"fastly increasing.\" More than half of all locations in the area have been evacuated, with most spots serving as afternoon 911 services. The agency warns such evacuations could harm the environment and risk lives. The Fire Department said in a press release that the 911 service at the ends of the fire center has all been suspended as of Tuesday, but will begin resuming the ambulance service Wednesday morning. 911 service at the western end of the fire center has also been suspended because of problems related to handling emergency calls to other areas, the release said. The service will remain active through the afternoon, and it will remain active through Wednesday, he said. John Sonny, national executive director of the Fire Department, said work is expected to resume on a weekly basis this week, but work is expected to begin next weekend, and will likely be held until mid-August. If that does not happen, he said the 911 service should be resumed in the afternoon for a more efficient response to the fire or if anything happens. There may be more response by early Monday, Sonny said, but the 911 service should be resumed until Thursday. The Brooklyn Fire Department said operations at its East View Fire District facility will remain active through Friday until changes are made informed.."
