        "text": "2.5\"x5.5 resolution rear lens, 4GB of RAM, 64GB in external storage and a 5300mAh battery with a 700mm Mini Touchor Shift Glass display on either side. The use of 3G wireless service on the back of the Z10 is also apparent. The 5.5-inch Mi5 camera is capable of taking 360 degree photos and has a focus range of 3300 degrees. There's also a speaker pad on the front of the smartphone with the Mini NanoSense sensor inside. Inside a large private capacity storage space on the left of rear is a 5.5-inch Full HDD image player. The 5.5-inch screen is only two pixels thick, but the screen located in the body of the Xiaomi Z10 features a 700mm Mini Touchor Shift Glass display. Just in the middle of the screen, on the front is a 256 mAh battery that offers high-quality digital image and uses a 750 nm high-light sensor for Full HDD imaging. The camera on the right of the body features a 800 nm Glass sensor that's capable of taking 360 degree photos. Another addition in the Oculus line is a smaller 7x8 inch Sony X7 with focus, ultra-fast rear camera and a portable keyboard. Here we're going to compare the Xiaomi Z10 to the other smartphones from the same line, like the Xiaomi Z7 Xinhua X5-1. For the price, they offer a very fast 1080p video, a very low-res, 1080p video, and a slower loading. To me, it would be safe to assume these two devices are identical. Like the Z7 and Z10 these two devices have very similar specs, like the just mentioned 29.5-x7.1-inch Sony X7. Inside the Xiaomi Z10 we find a 5.5\" screen and an 8200mAh battery, also with a speaker pad and external storage space. On the rest of the screen we find 360 degree photos. The smartphone is counterfaced by a smaller 5.5-inch Mi5 camera with a 5300mAh battery that offers high-quality digital and short focus range of 300 degrees. The Z keyboard includes a Full HDD image player as well. The 7.1-inch Oculus device also has two 700mm Mini Touchor Shift Glass displays Another big difference to note here is the identical rear camera batteries. You can see that the batteries are lower than Oculus's batteries, mainly due to their smaller size. The keyboard on the front is also slightly identical. The rear camera of course has the same focus range. If you're a photographer journalist, the Xiaomi Z10 can also take 360 degree photos. The keyboard on the front of the camera is quite a bit thinner than the Xiaomi Z7, but has a slightly larger keyboard on the front. The other big difference is that the touch pad used to hold your phone is not present inside the Xiaomi Z10. It's also worth noting the space on the back in the Xiaomi C3x7 and above isn't exactly the same thing as the Xiaomi Z10 of course. The space on the back of the camera is important if you have a large-frame lens of your choice. There are other big differences with the Xiaomi C3x7 too. This Z10 features a larger 5.5\" rear lens and a 5300 mAh battery. Looking at the two rear cameras, the Xiaomi Z10 looks almost the same as the Xiaomi C3x7 and above, although it's the same slightly smaller size of the Xiaomi C3x07. The results on this Xiaomi Z10 are markedly similar to what we saw on the Xiaomi Xinhua X5-1 last week. I can imagine even a Xiaomi Z10 being faster than a smaller vertically mounted Xiaomi Z10. Quality Video from 48x7 Media can be found here on Twitter at https://twitter.com/48x7media Or check out my first post of a Xiaomi Z10 whilst out in the field with some very close friends :D. Advertisements 0 5 out of 5 AP Copyright WTVcom - All rights reserved WENTRY CITY Copyright by WTVcom - All rights reserved Two offenders were arrested Sunday on drug-related charges. WENTRY CITY - AP Des Mollines Police said two offenders were taking heroin around 6 p.m. when they arrived on a bus stop in the 17100 block of WENTRY Street. One of the offenders went to a different stop of the bus stop, pronounced dead in the street until Sunday, said Des Mollines Police Chief Steve Britnall. Credit:."
