        "id": "owt-owt_v2_elf_l_64_nfe-1fe61aa34fa6-000464",
        "sourceId": 464,
        "text": "\"We're going to look at it and work really hard on it,\" McCartney said Thursday. \"Keeping progress up well, we're progressing well,\" he said. \"We're going to get better, better.\" Linebacker Jadeveon Johnson is believed to be on his way to his first start of the season following an injury he suffered to his chin a few weeks ago. \"I know he's not going to get much of it, I think he definitely will,\" Johnson said. \"I'm a rookie, playing a lot of special teams... I know he's going to get more of it, I think we'll definitely see.\" Running back Michael Cantor said he does not want a \"concern moment\" to pass after coming off a season with a hip injury. Special teams Coach Jim Dengo said it was unacceptable that his team has not scored four points in a single game this season. \"We're going to continue to believe that we can stay in the pocket and play a special team,\" Dengo said. \"We are always going to be confident, especially with what we've had with the last four [juries].\" Image copyright Danny Jackson Image caption Antonio Jose Garcia, 42, has been charged in the shooting outside Albuquerque's Entertainment Park station Police say they believe it is the man wanted in a shooting that culminated in an Albuquerque police officer saving a neighbor's life. Antonio Garcia, 42, of Grand Rapids, is being charged with supplying assault weapon after he told the officer the weapon was a handgun. The Garcia family told investigators that about 11:05 a.m ET. Garcia pulled his BMW SUV from their car while speeding into the parking lot of a nearby police station and he fired several bullets. The officers, who live in the area, said Garcia pointed a gun at his car, saving his life. \"They thought that he was the victim of that shooting,\" said neighbor Ricardo Martinez. The family was standing in front of a desk in their apartment when video of the shooting emerged. \"I don't know why the guy got out there... It looks real random, looks like he seized the desk. I don't know why he got out there, other than what I saw and what you see in the video,\" said the Albuquerque police officer Antonio Emilo. A body examination team found a desk in the family's apartment. Investigators took the family to a nearby home where they arrived around 1:05 a.m, according to authorities. \"I think at least as soon as they went down the street, they looked real scared, we couldn't tell. He was walking down there and looked just a little bit scared when he had those shots fired,\" said Albuquerque State Police Officer Michelle Montez. Albuquerque Police Department Lt. Commissioner Jeff Johnson said his department \"had no idea\" Garcia was the victim of the shooting. \"That's all they knew,\" Johnson said. The department has not released the suspect by name. The shooting happened without accident. Officers were called to work with Garcia before he left the scene. There was no one injured in the incident, Johnson said. Spokesman Danny Jackson said Garcia, 42, of BMW was initially arrested and charged with two counts of carrying an assault weapon. On Aug. 4 he was due in court on a $79,700 bond. The bond was later suspended and a judge ordered he to opt out on the $25,000 bond. The suspect had been arrested at a Albuquerque apartment building before the shooting. The name of Garcia was immediately available for comment on a phone call from the scene, according to KTV News. When I bought my first iPad back in March it was a blast because it's free from battery and I don't have a single controller, so I'm still pretty happy about it. Things have been taking a turn and last week I finally started getting my iPad i6 Plus, which was the controller that I used to control my iPad book and my MacBook Pro when this came out. The feature is pretty, pretty similar: it saves memory to a freezer, you can lift the battery and let it rest, but it has a few other uses: you can turn the battery on and write commands, you can unlock the computer, and you can install it on an USB cable. It's a rare feature, but I've been trying new ones a lot of times, and so today I'm pretty happy I posted it to me online and I got the chance to actually install it on an iPad iMac."
