        "id": "owt-owt_v2_elf_l_64_nfe-1fe61aa34fa6-000698",
        "sourceId": 698,
        "text": "Professor Maranne Martinez of the University of Florida stated that 2 years of genome sequencing made it possible to combat the spread of diseases such as BI and ALS in plants. By performing 3 years of genome sequencing, the researchers able to modify the DNA expression in humans by immutating these genes and propagating them to other generations. “This technique is highly effective because of the small amount of DNA it contains, but it is difficult to implement,” said study leader Pa Rajan, assistant professor in the Department of Neurochemistry of the University of Florida “The main objective of the current study was to create a proof-of-concept database of available diseases. We then isolated a small fragment of DNA (>2,000 mRNA) from a human genome to identify and modify other genes that are expressing the same disease.” The new Nintendo Gear Pro 3 is now valued at a price of $60 million in Japan, after Nintendo held a Tokyo-only press conference to announce the device. Additionally, Japanese official news agency Masommi published a short article on design and manufacturing on July 11. Japanese news newspaper Miyadi Koramieno has reported that design and manufacturing of the new Gear Pro 3 will begin in Japan in the fourth quarter of 2018, the newspaper reported. Design and manufacturing of the new Nintendo Gear Pro 3 is now expected to begin in the fourth quarter of 2018, according to the newspaper. The company has indicated that details of the new Nintendo Gear Pro 3 have not been finalized but will be unveiled in Japan at a later press conference. Additionally, the official Nintendo announcement was made on July 11 after Japanese news agency Masommi published a short article on design and manufacturing. Masommi published an image of the unveiled device under the headline, “Alcom Christmas to Nintendo,” as it revealed the new Nintendo Gear Pro 3. The new Gear Pro 3 is being offered as a replacement for the Nintendo DSDS Gear N Pro 3. The Nintendo Gear Pro 3 is based on Mario Earth 2, with the Nintendo logo. This marks the second week after Nintendo announced the Nintendo Gear Pro 3 and Japanese company Takaya has confirmed fresh announcements of the new Gear Pro 3 are coming in the country. “We’re very excited to have announced the new Nintendo Gear Pro 3,” said Takaya CEO Sarah Cohen at a press conference opening this morning. “We are quite excited about this new device.” Other features have been new to the Gear Pro 3, namely a bigger 13-inch-thall screen, a bigger 360-pixel camera, and slightly better performance than the Gear Pro 3. Developed by Takaya’s Chinese division, the Gear Pro 3 was announced at the Tokyo Electronic Arts Show on July 4. Given the power used on Nintendo’s flagship console, customers can expect it to cost significantly compare to the price of the Gear Pro 3 itself. Regular reports now indicate the device will go on sale in Japan in the next 3-5 days. (Top image via Reuters) President Trump tells White House press secretary Jay Bannon that he has not developed any plans for the Republican majority in the Senate. President Trump tells White House press secretary Jay Bannon that he has not developed any plans to secure the Republican majority in the Senate. (AP Photo/Caroel Ross, Benoit Gillard, AP) WASHINGTON — Presidential nominee Donald Trump on Friday lalashed out at Sen. John McCain (R-AZ) on immigration, saying he was engaged in \"no one great thing\" to secure the Republican majority in the Senate. \"We really've got to go back to the days and try to figure out what we're going to do,\" the president said on \"Face the Nation\" while describing a long list of goals he set for the Senate majority in 2016, including a health care overhaul, a government shutdown and cut taxes. \"If we want to win in the Senate, we really need to win,\" Trump said, adding that six more projects are in the works. \"We have to do the right thing.\" Trump has yet to lay out the details of McCain's plans. \"There's not one great thing here,\" he said during an address in front of the Senate Energy and Commerce Caucus on Thursday. McCain has made scores of policy statements, including in 2009, when he said he would prevent a government shutdown. But Bannon has yet to unveil a specific plan to stop the shutdown. In 2011, he made clear his intent to prevent a government shutdown, telling lawmakers in R.S.I. that his plan to prevent the shutdown is no longer necessary. \"But the thing is that we have to go back to days like that and try to figure out how to do the right thing,\" Trump said. \"That's where this is going to end up being.\""
