        "id": "owt-owt_v2_elf_l_64_nfe-1fe61aa34fa6-001013",
        "sourceId": 1013,
        "text": "The company sells books and ebooks from a book store in the neighborhood, and plans to keep them in Green Bay and Milwaukee. The Smiths and Cohen stores that built the single-storey facility at 339 W. MIT St. have all been sold off, Lawll said. Lawll plans to keep the facility in Milwaukee, from an older single-storey building at 360 W. MIT St. He said the transformation work is still ongoing. “It’s more than a one-bed facility,” he said. “It’s a retail facility.” Owners want space for art “I want owners to have a space and location where they can store their own artwork. They’ve been doing that for 18 years, and they want to have new stores there, Lawll said. Eric Serina, who has lived in the neighborhood for a decade and a half, said he cares about art and publishing. “We are a creatively led community. It has an excellent history,” Serina said. “Everyone gets it.” With the Falcons attracting enormous interest, Atlanta offensive lineman Aaron Rodgers said he doesn't expect to miss a chance at a Graham Stadium game in Denver on Saturday night. The Falcons kick off at 3 a.m. PDT on Saturday, with a 34-17 wild-card win over the Patriots. Speaking to the Atlanta Business Tribune, Rodgers said the Patriots are nearly as aggressive as their defensive counterparts, with a 41-41 win over the Washington Redskins and Texans. \"They're playing some really good football. I think I can enjoy those games,\" he said. \"Not all games have been fantastic. But they're taking a lot of fun out of what they're displaying.\" \"I don't think anyone is going to be able to watch,\" Rodgers said. \"I'm really satisfied with how well they're playing this season. I don't think anyone is going to be able to go and watch a single game. I really like the Falcons. I think they're doing well and I'm sure I can see them going well.\" The Falcons return to the NFC North Atlantic for the NFC Championship Game, and face the No. 4 Patriots in the NYF round with a 5-8 record. The Falcons won't take a snap on the home field against the San Francisco 49ers. Round 3 begins at 1 a.m. PDT The Patriots are not yet playing at the normal pace for Tom Brady, who is in the midst of the summer of rehab after a series of injuries to his left ankle. Brady is in the middle of the season with the NFL's Nate Worms so far. The Falcons won't be spending most of their season at Graham Stadium on Saturday when they head to Atlanta, so wouldn't be able to miss a game against the Washington Redskins or the Cincinnati Bengals that will begin Oct. 26. * * * * Posted on 20 April 2009 Microsoft Entertainment Inc. is very excited to announce the release of its PC port, College Play Mode for Windows, iOS and Linux. The next-generation PC port, College Play Mode is a portable PC gaming program that lets you download games from your PS4 or Xbox 360 or even your phone and tablet over the course of a few hours. It means you can purchase and play multiple games on your PC at no cost. Many of the competing PC titles are incredibly expensive, due to the fact that your PC can play up to 15 games per week. Some take a minimum of almost six hours to play. With College Play Mode, you can purchase multiple competing titles and take advantage of many competing PC titles at an inflated price. Many competing PC titles, such as Wonderland, Dream Island, Heavennight and The Ironmaid, are monetizated with College Play Mode. For those who enjoy digital-money gaming, they don’t have to wait long to find some of the best print titles. It’s a convenient way to discover competing PC titles and make your casual PC gaming interest a reality. For more information about College Play Mode, see our press release. Microsoft: Windows An interactive game-playing program, College Play Mode will have you playing game-to-game with four different players on the same screen. It’s a fun-filled program with its eye-opening gameplay, multi-tasking mechanics, and an eight-player display. College Play Mode will help become one of the best shooters in the world to catch a ball, stop an attack, and win a national championship award. For more information about College Play Mode, see our press release. Apple: Windows"
