        "sourceId": 46,
        "text": "“The identification of these problems is strongly influenced by a number of approaches to neuronal research,” Singapore University psychologist Jiang Zong said in a prepared statement. “The extent to which the research tasks is restricted is not always appropriate. resolving neuronal network limitations required to complete these tasks — for example, by exploring the interactions between individual neurons, tracking them through 3-D magnetography, and comprehensive energy expression analysis — is necessary for ensuring the stable and secure operating of neuronal networks.” Apple has announced that it will be displaying an iPhone 4C device at startup conferences and tech events across the country. \"Deploying an iPhone 4C at tech events is a historic achievement,\" Apple CEO Tim Cook said in a statement on \"Gall Me.\" Earlier in the day, the company announced that it would be displaying the device at its \"Gell Me\" event in Atlanta. Apple will be displaying an iPhone 4C at tech events at its annual startup conference in Chicago. While the iPhone 4C may not be available for purchase, Apple has not officially announced a prototype device with a mouse yet. Amazon would still allow customers to purchase the iPhone 4C, which is the same as the iPhone X and doesn't require a mouse. The characteristics of the 4C are very similar to what Apple displayed when it launched the iPhone 5. The iPhone 4C has a better display, more flexible options, and extended battery life, but it's also restricted. Unlike the iPhone X, the 4C has power interfaces, but it doesn't require a mouse or mouse. It instead has a 5.5-inch, 480-hp battery with a new quad-core processor and 1,200mAh. It's not clear whether the 1,200mAh or 1,200mAh battery is available. Police accused of sexually assaulting a 24-year-old student after using a mask during class Garland Police have accused sexually assaulting a 24-year-old student inside her high school after using a mask during a class. Police say 44-year-old Karen Sullivan, 48-year-old Za Cruz and 32-year-old Blake Subhone are accused of sexual assault and second-degree assault. The incident occurred shortly after 8 p.m. Thursday at Garland County High School. Sullivan said Sullivan was inside the class when the other student grabbed her. “She said it was a little odd, and she felt a little sorry about it,” Sullivan said. “But once she got into the class, she went. She didn’t feel a whole bad about it.” Sullivan was taken into custody. Police are still investigating the circumstances of the incident. Sullivan was pronounced dead at a Galves County hospital facility. According to Garland Police Capt. Jared Sullivan, all three officers were on duty at the time of the incident. According to Sullivan, Sullivan was sitting in the front row of the class. “It was a little odd, and it was pretty busy,” Sullivan said. “She was going up to a chair and shouting, ‘I’m sorry!’ and just talking about, ‘Can I see your eyes?’ And then, the other student came up and grabbe her.” Sullivan said as police entered the class, Sullivan grabbed her by the chair and dropped her to the ground. “She was sitting in the front row of the class,” Sullivan said. Police ask anyone to contact a Crime Detective at (202) 461-3100. Update: This story originally reported information regarding Garland County High School. JIC - UN has requested formal resolution on Palestinian settlements \"The United Nations has today requested a formal resolution on Israel's Palestinian settlements on the Hamavic Temple in Jerusalem,\" Ayatollallah Barak-usmar, an official from the UN's High Commissioner for Human Rights, told the Israeli television network. The Israeli television said that the UN has been able to condemn 14 of Israel's settlements, including in Lebanon, Egypt, Somalia, Jordan, and Yemen, but has yet to yet receive the formal resolution. \"The resolution on the Palestinian dispute is required by international humanitarian law,\" UN Secretary General Ban Ki-mun said in a statement. The UN has the authority to demand an end to the settlements until Israel intervenes in a manner of ending the dispute, the statement said. \"It is the responsibility of the UN to request a formal resolution until Israel intervens in a manner of achieving a peaceful solution to the dispute and preventing the persecution and enslavement of residents,\" the statement said. Israel regularly holds public protests against the settlements on the Hamavic Temple, in East Jerusalem."
