        "id": "owt-owt_v2_elf_m_128_nfe-16ea6daeb24f-000577",
        "sourceId": 577,
        "text": "Phil McCrory has already been nominated for a Rolling Stone Actor Award for his roles in TV shows like The Sheriff and All Night. Phil McCrory has already been nominated for two Golden Actor nominations after playing Sheriff Scott Carter & John McKenzie. David Goldberger David Goldberger is best known for his work on the TV series The Twice. He has already been nominated for a Golden Screen Actor Award for playing Jim Young, Bruce Westmore, Chuck Hefburn, Peter Burnazi, Paul Mosa, Paul Heath & Brian McGrath. David Korel David Korel has already been nominated for two Golden Emmy nominations, not least for his work in films including The Imposter and Miraf Kroub Korel has already been nominated for the Golden Actor Award for having played Josh Hunter, Leopold Nelson, John Duke & Andrew Lanbury. Chad Korel has also been nominated for a Rolling Stone Actor Award for playing Kevin Ramford & Deb Cooper. Paul Coulter Paul Coulter is best known for his work on the children's comedy Ninja Gold, where he has received consecutive Golden Emmy nominations. He can also be seen in Mike Vaughan's film The Imposter, playing the protagonist in the cinematic adventure The Mislords. Golden Emmy Screenshots Paul McCabeth, director in new FBI probe into Donald Trump's campaign Golden Screen Paul McCabeth, director in new FBI probe into Donald Trump's presidential campaign Follow me on Twitter WASHINGTON (AP) — A memo sent Wednesday to FBI Director Trey McMaster, part of a document about the agency's probe to the Senate Judiciary Committee, was first reported by the Washington Post. Director Trey McMaster, chairman of the Senate Judiciary Committee, is next scheduled to comment publicly on a U.S. special operations probe shared with the FBI into the Russian government and Donald Trump's financial activities during the 2016 presidential campaign. The Mcmaster memo comes just over a week after a June 5 memo from FBI Director Anthony Everett and FBI Director ScottPriitt detailing the payments and contributions of the Trump campaign's director and national security adviser Michael Flynn, former White House national security adviser James Kushner, and former Russian President Victor Yanukovich were also mentioned in the memo sent on Wednesday. It comes just a few days after a memo from Mcmaster to national security adviser Michael Flynn and White House national security adviser James Kushner detailing how Flynn's financial activities were encouraged by the Donald Trump campaign. State polling records show that Flynn, a founding member of the South Carolina Republican Party, was given money by the Russian government and various other entities affiliated with the Trump campaign, and spent at least $200 million during the 2016 presidential election cycle, the FBI said as part of its ongoing investigation into Trump. Mcmaster memo is part of a wide-ranging probe into Flynn's money given to him by the Russian government and other entities affiliated with the Trump campaign, a key step in the ongoing investigation into Trump's involvement in the 2016 election and his alleged collusion with Russia. The memo await a final confirmation hearing from the Senate Judiciary Committee. Topics: presidential-election, prosecution, law-crime-and-justice, federal-government, tyney-priitt, britley, buckland, post, melany, dotland-captain, ootland-1770, melany First posted Carolina Hurricanes quarterback Peter Horsmink has agreed to a long-term contract extension with the division champion New Jersey Coyotes, according to a source obtained from SpitchFootball. Horsmink signed the contract extension on July 26, but Horsmink has not disclosed any release dates. The Hurricanes are likely to not sign him until the end of the season before signing him to free agency, according to the same source. Unlike Darry Vogger, the Hurricanes are interested in playing an offensive lineman who would be a natural first-round pick. A contract extension would give the team more flexibility to bring in a new offensive lineman for Horsmink. The team also is interested in acquiring Eric Schmell, Isaiah Sazaroth and DeAndrean Woodard. In addition, due to Horsmink's ability to play on the run, the Hurricanes would need a new offensive lineman who would be signed by the end of next year's season."
