        "text": "DNC President Ben Heparad vetoed another recent proposal to raise the minimum wage to $15.25 for parents with children from ages 16 to 18. He said every parent should be entitled to a living wage of $115 if their children are over the age of 18. \"It's really counter-productive to leave them with a living wage,\" said DNC President Claire Dianna, who vetoed several of the proposals. Wsington and nearby cities — such as Madison City and Baltimore — are expected to vote on the proposals next week. Dianna can be reached at de.dianna@wsington.com or 818-363-8987. Community meetings and debates will take place from 9 a.m. p.m. on Wednesday at the headquarters of the City Council. The City Council in Madison City, Christington, Baltimore and Statenington are expected to vote on the proposals Wednesday. \"There's a complicated debate during these meetings,\" said John Preett, the assistant district attorney for Wsington. \"So we need to vote today to end that debate.\" Heparad has already vetoed another proposal to raise the local minimum wage to $15.25 and said it would be worth an extra $10 a month for the average family. The world's largest video game distributor says it's bringing a revised version of the critically-acclaimed Star Trek: Deep Discovery game to the Play Store to make its version of the game accessible to a wide range of consumers. Occulus Video Games have announced the update, which today includes a new version of the game, along with tweets from Amazing Media's Jason Middleman and Star Trek VP Jerry Wilson. \"We wanted to make a game that will be accessible to allages and be sure to appeal to a wide range of consumers,\" said Occulus VP Jerry Wilson. \"With our first-ever game, we've always wanted to give everyone an experience in a video game experience while at the simultaneously time being able to reach consumers all over the world.. This update provides such an awesome experience; we've always wanted to serve all people playing this game, especially in Netflixs that have recently come to the market. We take great pride on allowing people of allages and sizes the opportunity to enjoy playing this awesome game via our Netflix Channel.\" Star Trek: Deep Discovery Pay-To-Play \"Occulus Video Games takes the opportunity to high-optimise their Star Trek: Deep Discovery gameplay experience with a powerful update, which includes content from a wide range of tournaments, tournaments, and party genres. Occulus has also added multiplayer content from various party genres such as Battle Zone 2, Metro Center 2 and Star Warcry 3, Finality Storm. We've always wanted to give everyone an experience in a video game experience, especially in Netflixs that have recently come to the market.\" Exitowing the world's first video game \"We wanted to make a game that will be accessible to people of allages and sizes while at the simultaneously time being able to reach consumers all over the world. The update provides such an awesome experience. Using Netflix Channel, we're so excited to work with Occulus to try to make a game that will not only be readable to allages but that will serve every age in a brilliant way,\" Star Trek VP Jerry Wilson said in a statement. Star Trek: Deep Discovery Resize Limited Edition \"We’re excited to bring an updated version of Star Trek: Deep Discovery Resize, the Star Trek gameplay update that was released last night for $9.99 on iPhone and Android devices, to the Play Store. This update includes all of the Star Trek: Deep Discovery gameplay modes, as well as an updated gameplay schedule for Star Trek episodes.\" Fans of Star Trek episodes that aren’t ready yet can sign up for the update today at the Play Store. The Play Store version of Star Trek: Deep Discovery Resize is available today, for $9.99 on iPhone 4, PlayStation 4, Android and Wii U. With the update, new Star Trek gameplay modes will be available for preorder. A complete Star Trek: Deep Discovery gameplay schedule, a list of upcoming updates, and much more information is available at www.star Trekdoss.com. Star Trek: Deep Discovery Resize Limited Edition Star Trek: Deep Discovery creator Darlen Lanceb is working on an update for the Star Trek Limited Edition which is scheduled for release on November 1, 2018. Star Trek: Deep Discovery Pay-To-Play for iPhone 4, Wii U and PC Star Trek: Deep Discovery creator Darlen Lanceb is working on an update for the Star Trek Limited Edition which is scheduled for release on November 1, 2018. Star Trek: Deep Discovery"
