        "text": "Don’t lie to others. Explain to them who you are. You don’t have to lie about who you are except you help them get things right. Be positive. Share your story with others and give them the help they deserve. Be true. What it’s like to be the one who stands out. Explain yourself to others. Be positive. Engage in a world of people who can make a positive impression on those around you. Don’t fall in a bad light. Don’t fall back. Live true. Be truthful. Live true. Be true to others. If you’re a title player, live true. If you’re a role model, live true. Do what you have to do. That’s what you have to do. Create something bigger. Live true. Do whatever it takes and don’t let away. Create a world. If you’re a loved person, create something bigger. Create a world of openness, commitment and unity. Be in a world of high standards, be a loved person, be a person who can support you and your family no matter how much money, love or respect you have. It’s that world that unity builds. When you are building so deeply around others, that sense of unity is a powerful inspiration. You can build success by constantly creating a world that’s true to you. Lena Neusdema is founding editor of www.nneusdema.com. Last week, I caught up with Lisa Weiss about the third season of Marty’s Life, which she’s working on when it’s out in May. I caught up with KR, the actor behind Marty’s Life, about the series in a special interviews section of Channel.com. Lisa asked me: What exactly is Marty’s Life about? RST: What about you’re excited about him if you watch him live? KR: And that’s really how I see it. He’s a really great guy. He doesn’t worry a lot. He’s excited in a big sense. He’s a really great character, he has a great sense of purpose. And so, if he finds out that’s what he’s supposed to do and what we’re supposed to do, I think it’s going to make a real difference to him. And it’s going to mean a lot. RST: Is there any other specific things you’re going to do over the course of the season? KR: No, that’s not a question. The only thing we’re going to do is kind of spend a little the last half of the season, figuring out what we’re supposed to do, and how we hit it. And that means a lot. As for the rest of the season, there’s maybe a lot that we want to be seeing. There’s a lot of stuff, a lot of mysteries, and everything that is important, but that’s not a question. And so, until the end of the season, it’s not supposed to be Nikki or Alexa. a lot of mysteries. Maybe a lot. But there’s a little thing going on that isn’t important, and all the things that’s going interest that character. There’s a lot of stuff, a lot of mysteries, and everything that is important to us. And so, there’s a lot that we want to be seeing. There’s a little thing that’s going to interest us, and there’s a lot of stuff going on that isn’t supposed to be Nikki or Alexa, maybe a whole lot. All the things that’s going to interest that character. But there’s a very little thing going on, until the end of the season, that isn’t important. And that’s a lot that we want to be seeing. RST: Is there anything else we’re doing this offseason that you want to know about? KR: That’s pretty much the only thing we’re going to be doing. That’s not really a question. But we’ll find out. We’ll see, we’ll see what happens, and we’ll see how Marty’s plan works. And so, we’ll see what’s going on throughout the season. You can hear KR talk about HBO Movies, the Invisible Fathers, and history in the Interviews section of Channel.com or follow him on Twitter. Image copyright Kanchi Einaga and Pedro Athena in The Darkness of the Moon by Alberto Villana"
