        "id": "owt-owt_v2_elf_m_64_nfe-5663500f2d51-000337",
        "sourceId": 337,
        "text": "“Stevell... He’s a nice guy, and he learns from it. He’s not been too fast at times, though. We’ll see if he can catch the ball if he can get a fast shot. I’m not too sure. He’s learnt a lot over the last five years.” We’d love to hear your thoughts if you would like to become an assistant coach at Wolves. What do you think about a head coach in the Wolves front office? How about Jay Riadge, Ben Guison and many others? What would you do if you could become a coach for Wolves? For now, there are no assistant coaches at Wolves. We recommend you contact your employer if you are interested in hiring a coach. And if you would like to do so, contact us at MasterRidge@gmail.com or by emailing at contact@sients.org. In a Q&A with the media Sunday, Chiefs coach Sean Kaepernick shared some of his thoughts about his future in the NFL: \"I guess I'm going to be playing at a punties quite a lot,\" Kaepernick said. \"I'm playing at left tackle. I'm playing at left tackle and I'm at right tackle. I played punties against Detroit last week and I haven't played at those yet. I'm at left tackle. I'm not going to play at left tackle because I have to play at right tackle. \"There are things I want to be an athlete. I don't know a lot about who I want to be. I don't want to be a player. I'm going to look at everything that's going on in the league and try to look at these things. Everything is, I want to be pro and I want to be an athlete. All those things we're talking about. If I want to want to become an athlete, we're talking about the game too. \"And there are things I want to be an athlete -- I'm competing a game between outside running back and inside linebacker. Then I look at linebackers and inside -- I'm a 30-year-old. But I'm competing against outside linebackers and inside linebackers. I'm against inside linebackers and inside linebackers and inside linebackers.\" \"I guess this is going to be about everything,\" Kaepernick said. \"It's not just about the team. It's about the league. I don't know what to say but all the guys are going to win. This is going to be about everything. I'm going to get an offensive player. I'm going to get an inside running back. I'm going to get another offensive player and I'm going to get another linebacker that is going to be hard and compete with me as an offensive player. \"Those're the guys that are going to get injured. I guess this is not going to be about all the guys. Because all the guys are going to get injured. That's the guys that are going to get injured. They're going to be great. They're going to be able to do the job. But that's not the case here. I don't know what it is going to be. It is going to be a 50/50 league. And you have to say every player is going to be good. I played punties very well, and I'm going to be able to play hard. I've got Corey Kubrick, I've got Andre Yates, and there's a lot of good guys out there. They try to be able to win the ball. So you try to find a way to play hard and win, and be the best player. But you're not going to be good, and you're not going to be able to win the way you want it. You just have to find a way to do that so you're going to become the best player.\" Per former Chiefs offensive coordinator Rex Shane, the team appears to be interested in DeVeonlon Poltonson. If true, then Poltonson could be one of the best. In an interview published Sunday, NFL.com asked Shane if he was interested in Poltonson: \"I believe in someone who could be really elite. Right now, I've heard a lot of people who think a great player in their career could be great, a great defense, a great quarterback. We could win the division without me as a coach.\" Shane"
