        "id": "owt-owt_v2_elf_m_64_nfe-5663500f2d51-000422",
        "sourceId": 422,
        "text": "If you want to hire an architectural expert or manager with a goal of enhancing performance and productivity in your workplace, there are a number of great options out there. You can define any architectural goal you want to achieve in your current workplace, find the right architectural software to maintain a building, or pick the right software that is responsible for a business line or operating system. This software can also be used as a reference sheet to compare performance of your architectural goals, for example. The right software can also be used to improve the look and feel of a office structure. The right software can also be used to lower the overall operability and maintenance costs of a structure, as well as make it easier for employees to take care of the whole structure themselves. There are many emerging architectural techniques out there that capitalize on the flexibility of a complex office structure, such as solar-powered display lighting, steel climb-based commutators, and improvements in high-tech hardware. Together, all of these techniques can have a profound impact on an organization’s performance and can produce a dramatic reduction in labor costs, so figuring out the right strategy can work for all of your employees. AttributeBest has identified the iPhone 6 S6 as the world's top 100 Android phone — and in particular, the other S6 phones far with even higher new world rankings. We've also created a chart that breaks down the phones' rankings below. In fact, the iPhone 6 S7 and iPad 6 are the world's top 100 Android phones, followed by the iPhone 6 S 7, Apple iPhone 6 S8, Apple iPhone 6 Plus and Apple iPhone 6 Plus. Check out the world's top 100 Android phones on both the iPhone 6 S7 and iPhone 6 S6, and repeat the chart below to see how the iPhone 6 S7 and iPad 6 fared in the top 100. Keep up with the latest computer and tech news, and make sure to follow us on Facebook and Twitter! CAPORTALIX — The couple must have registered to marry as a person who is a gay man or a lesbian, a California lawyer for the married couple has said. Conor MacKenley and Claire Cropman launched a petition on Facebook to promote a law passed last month that would allow the federal government to legally register same sex marriage as one of nine legal entities to obtain all marriage permits, license papers, marriage permits and employment records. The law passed by a unanimous vote Dec. 15, marking the first time Congress has allowed the state to pass a law on the issue of same sex marriage. MacKenley, who served in the second administration of President Barack Obama, said, “Endending equal rights for everyone is the goal here, and we must fight for it.” The couple is passionately behind the law. “It is time for Congress take up its power to ensure that gay and les people have equal opportunity to marry openly and legally,” MacKenley said. “Our Foundation is dedicated to improving marriage equality for LGBT people and supporting LGBT rights in the United States.” While California does not officially position with the federal government on the issue of same sex marriage, the state’s position on equal rights in darriage is constitutionally unproledged. The petition from MacKenley and Cropman has almost 12,000 signatures in two days. A Dec. 19 statement from the petition reads, “We wholeheartedly support the decision of the state’s highest court to overturn the Supreme Court’s ruling in Ladies United v. USA in 2008 that opened the door for same sex marriage in the state. As the proud ladies of a same-sex couple, both the state and federal government recognize California’s rules on same sex marriage as an important issue. We truly believe that same sex marriage should also be part of California’s rules.” A footnote from the petition says, “At the moment, courts all over the country seem to allow gay couples to marry outside their state. However, recent rulings by the State of California and the District of Columbia have changed attitudes toward same sex marriage.” The petition also asks the couple to register as a same-sex person on the grounds that she is “a transmarried or a gay or a lesbian.” Send tips to dwis@dilycaller Content created by The Daily Caller News Foundation is available without charge to any eligible news publisher that can provide a large audience. For licensing opportunities of our original content, please contact licensing@dailycallernewsfoundation.org. This may be sent to dwis@dilycaller.com or 1-800-888-9277. More on LGBT rights from Speaking Out!, the Divorce Law Center and Diversity Watch."
