        "id": "owt-owt_v2_elf_m_64_nfe-5663500f2d51-000675",
        "sourceId": 675,
        "text": "I had recently asked our long-time blog developer, Matti Wright, to develop a mobile app. He uses a mobile device that allows him to instantly comment on a blog that we've been talking for the past few months. Matti and I have found dozens of commentary apps and blogs and web pages, so we agreed to create a comment board. How did we come up with this idea? Matti created a system for developers to create comment boards from scratch where you can use your phone to add or remove a comment board and activate the comment board. The creation of comment boards took a long time, but this system proved to be labor intensive and expensive. The creation of comment board boards represent a step toward Matti's vision. This system will allow developers to create mobile apps for small organizations and larger businesses. Each app has a comment board, which allows you to tell your users about the app. It's like how many comment board apps will look: As your apps get popular, you'll be able to use them as you interact with your business. Each comment board will have a \"Complaint Board banner\" built into your desktop, allowing you to display the app over your social media platforms or using a mobile mobile device. It allows developers to keep track of how many users use a comment board. Comment board banners will enable developers to build innovative applications using new technology by creating new comment boards that can display your comments, likes, likes, and even social stats. After working with Matti to create a comment board, I started to notice a lot of problems that developers face when working with bloggers. These ones, we call the \"blog pages problem.\" Typically, developers don't build apps to set up commentary on blogs or other websites. So after working with Matti, we continued to look for applications that can help engage developers. To accomplish Matti's vision, we set out to develop apps that enable commentary on a wide range of topics. Eventually, we created a mobile web application that allows your blog to host posts on a range of topics. Then, we created a user-friendly platform that allows your phone to host the topics on your blog. Working with Matti spearheaded the development of image-based commenting One of the first topics that attracted our attention in the mobile phone space was in image-based commenting. Working with Matti, we invented a platform that allowed developers to interact with bloggers and explore how users could make choices using their apps. Together with Matt, we developed our mobile app that is based on a blog-post platform that offers commentary that can be done directly by mobile phones. This app allows us to deliver commentary by highlighting a specific set of topics in real time or by judging on a natural rendered image. With a help of our image-based and commenting bots, we were able to figure out specifically which of these bots to use for image-based commentary. A lot of people use a bot for commenting on a topic, and we realized that the best way of presenting a commenting post is to choose the article topic, and then open up your blog, saving your running time and computing costs. At the same time in developing the platform, we learned that each visit to a image-based commenting edits your blog page in the same way as a natural image. The platform allowed us to come up with specifically which commenting to use for. Working with it, we found a number good ways to take advantage of apps that allowed users to comment on specific topics, but our resources were limited at the time. It took us a bit of research to figure out how to take advantage of these applications, and we got there. Early mobile use We first thought of mobile phones as an option almost a decade ago. As mobile phones became the dominant of mobile devices, we gradually began to depend on integrated applications for both commentary and commenting. We would be able to add more new applications each day as we learned to add older ones through our commenting bots. With our years of experience in the commenting space, we were able to find inspiration and build powerful apps that could accomplish the task faster and smarter quickly. The following year, we launched and released the new Blog Commenting Tool, a mobile page development tool that allows developers to create apps for various kinds of tasks like highlighting popular images, likes, comments and so on. Virtually all of these applications come from bloggers; each single application generates millions of views. Each application is easily accessible to many developers, and the sheer number of applications that offer this kind of functionality is astonishing. This past May, a popular commentary app, blogSmartGive.com, garnered over 3 million downloads in a single day."
