        "text": "T:J: Well, I don't know if it's important. I don't think so. I think that's the most important thing. The right thing to do is focus on the game and enjoy it, and just keep practicing and playing it. I think that's one of the things that will help you practice and to practice and play it more. QAAB: Actually, after you toured both worlds, your work experience was different, or was that situation a little different, and how you feel about that experience? T:J: Yeah, I don't know. It's a great memory, but it helps me practice more. That's how I feel about it. QAAB: When did you get offered, or was it that you wanted to work for Jack Chawn? What did you expect? Did you still work for him or did you didn't spend time with him at all? QAAB: What was it like? T:J: Well, it was awesome. In the end, everything went according. I got an offer. Every time I put the offer on hold, I re-signed, and I had to figure out what to do, and it was really challenging for me to do that. I also think there was just a bit of bureaucracy inside me. QAAB: When did the offer arrive and what your life situation looked like? T:J: I don't know exactly, but I took a good chance to make the offer. QAAB: Can't you tell me a bit about that? T:J: Again, I had a lot of fun with Jack Chawn, and I wanted to take care of him in his own right. I wanted to miss him as much as I could because he felt like he's a good friend. After I got offered, I went on a tour with Jack Chawn and got to know him and just appreciate him, and I saw him at work on WrestleMania, and I felt like it was time to spend some extra time with him. Now, I just saw him at work on WrestleMania again. QAAB: You worked for Jack Chawn? T:J: I was lucky enough to miss Jack in that way. I had no idea if it was what I'm offered, so I thought I'd be willing to go out and work with someone. But I had a lot of respect for me in the same way, and I definitely missed him. QAAB: You guys, you have a trainer who's probably slightly smarter than the co-associates that you usually work with. Do you agree with that? T:J: Yeah, he really liked me. It was really fun to be working with him, actually. He's a good friend, and I wanted to have a lot of fun with him. It was really fun to be working with anyone. Just being like him and just thinking about him would have been a big deal, so I really enjoyed working with him, and just having a great amount of fun with him. I think since I've worked on the other tours, there has been quite a bit of an interest. And a lot of people aren't familiar with WrestleMania. Actually, there's lots of others interested, but I've never done anything on WrestleMania before, and I definitely enjoy working with him. QAAB: Won't you write him a letter to you? wouldn't you write him a letter too? T:J: Yeah, I wouldn't have been interested. I wouldn't have ever written him a letter or talked to me. It's just like, \"Thinks, oh.\". Because of that thing, I have a lot of emotions. I've worked on WrestleMania before, and it's getting better and better to spend time with him after he's done on WrestleMania. QAAB: There is another person you're excited about? T:J: No, it's this particular person of dominate, which not only happens spiritually, but also emotionally. It's just that he isn't going to be a perfect person yet. I like him a lot more. So, I'm definitely excited a lot about him. I think he's excited about more people than I am, and I'm definitely excited about this person, but right now I'm kinda excited about that. QAAB: If you describe yourself as the person that you worked for, do you feel like you dominate in a lot of people?"
